' 34a The blocks of the N4 merge with an empty sibling: the empty block is
' the main parent of the merge block, so the merge adds the space branch to
' the state of an empty block.
'
' Source of the N4 figure of ../verification.md (section 34.9), a
' sub-figure of figure 34. The figure restates the test
' n4_space_merge_with_empty_sibling of casper/tests/reified/n4.rs and the
' three facts of Casper of decision 82. It adds no new fact.
'
' Reading order, from the bottom to the top:
'   1. Node 0, the leader, proposes block A (payer 0 creates a queue space)
'      and block B (payer 1 creates a set space) on genesis.
'   2. Node 1 proposes the empty block E on genesis.
'   3. Node 2 receives A, B and E and proposes the merge block M. Its first
'      parent, the main parent, is E. The merge rejects no deploy.
'   4. Node 0 proposes block T on M: payer 0 touches its queue space. Every
'      node validates M and T, and T reads the queue of the space branch.
'
' Colors come from concept-colors.iuml (aliases of the shared palette).
' Render: ./render.sh 34a-n4-merge-dag.puml   Check: ./render.sh --check

@startuml 34a-n4-merge-dag
!include ../../../casper/theory/diagrams/palette.iuml
!include concept-colors.iuml
$ca_base_skin()
skinparam ArrowColor $rrs_relation
skinparam RectangleBorderColor $rrs_relation
skinparam NoteBorderColor $rrs_relation
skinparam LegendBorderColor $rrs_relation
skinparam LegendBackgroundColor $ca_note_grey
title The blocks of the N4 merge with an empty sibling

rectangle "**T**: node 0\npayer 0 touches its queue space\ndelivers the config, a take\nand a fired waiter" as T $rrs_storage
rectangle "**M**: merge block of node 2\nparents [E, B]\nno rejected deploy" as M $rrs_host
rectangle "**E**: node 1\nan empty block" as E $rrs_reserved
rectangle "**B**: node 0\npayer 1 creates a set space" as B $rrs_storage
rectangle "**A**: node 0\npayer 0 creates a queue space\nwith records and a waiter" as A $rrs_storage
rectangle "**genesis**\noffered v6, three validators,\ntwo searched payers" as G $rrs_host

T -[$rrs_relation]-> M : parent
M -[$rrs_effect,bold]-> E : main parent
M -[$rrs_relation,dashed]-> B : second parent
B -[$rrs_relation]-> A : parent
A -[$rrs_relation]-> G : parent
E -[$rrs_relation]-> G : parent

note right of M
The chains of the main parent never enter
a merge. With E as the main parent, the
merge applies the deploys of A and B to
the post-state of E, so the merge of the
space branch is not vacuous. Every node
validates M, and then T.
end note

note right of A
Leader rule: node 0 proposes every
space block. The cost-cursor buckets
of payers 0 and 1 are disjoint (DR-119),
so the branch has no cursor conflict.
end note

legend bottom
**Concept colors**
|<$rrs_storage>    | block with a space deploy |
|<$rrs_host>       | genesis and the merge block |
|<$rrs_reserved>   | empty block |
**Arrows**
|<$rrs_effect>     | main parent: the merge starts from its post-state |
|<$rrs_relation>   | parent |
endlegend
@enduml
